# What the safetensors runtime needs on a machine with a CUDA card, which is everything the
# base file lists plus the one thing that only means anything on a GPU.
#
# It is a separate input rather than an entry in requirements.in because that file compiles
# both lockfiles, and bitsandbytes on a machine with no CUDA is thirty six megabytes of
# binaries for cards it does not have. Four bit weights are refused outright there instead,
# which is the honest answer and the one the loader now gives.
-r requirements.in

# Four bit weights, which is what makes a model too large for a machine fit on it. Pinned to
# the first release carrying libbitsandbytes_cuda132.dll, matching the torch cu132 build this
# lockfile installs; 0.49.2 and earlier stop at CUDA 13.0 and have no binary for this one.
bitsandbytes==0.50.1
